<details id="draft-collection-panel" class="recovery-box">
<summary>Keep several articles in a private collection</summary>
<p id="draft-collection-help" class="small">Save up to eight workspaces in one private file. Add or update an article explicitly, then download the collection before leaving. Editing the article does not update its saved entry. This tab has no autosave or account history.</p>
<fieldset id="draft-collection-controls" disabled><legend class="sr-only">Private draft collection</legend>
<p id="draft-collection-count" class="small" role="status" aria-live="polite">0 / 8 saved articles in this tab.</p>
<label for="draft-collection-name">Saved article name</label><input id="draft-collection-name" maxlength="80" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="draft-collection-name-help"><p id="draft-collection-name-help" class="small">For a new entry, leave blank to use the current title. The name labels this saved workspace; it does not change your article title.</p>
<button id="add-to-draft-collection" type="button" class="secondary">Add current writing as a new saved article</button>
<section id="draft-collection-selection" hidden aria-labelledby="draft-collection-selection-heading">
<h2 id="draft-collection-selection-heading">Your saved articles</h2><label for="draft-collection-select">Saved article to inspect or open</label><select id="draft-collection-select"></select><p id="draft-collection-selected-status" class="small" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
<details id="draft-collection-inspection"><summary>Inspect the selected private workspace</summary><label for="draft-collection-saved-preview">Saved writing and notes, in workspace JSON format</label><textarea id="draft-collection-saved-preview" rows="8" readonly spellcheck="false"></textarea></details>
<div class="actions"><button id="open-draft-collection-entry" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Open selected article in the editor</button><button id="update-draft-collection-entry" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Update selected from current writing</button><button id="rename-draft-collection-entry" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Rename selected article</button><button id="remove-draft-collection-entry" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Remove selected saved article</button></div>
</section>
<button id="undo-draft-collection" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Undo last collection change</button><p class="small">Undo recovers one add, update, rename, removal, or collection load. It changes saved entries only. Opening an article keeps valid current writing in Revisions and clears export approval and publishing profiles. Workspace restore and imports keep this collection. Clear this writing desk removes the collection, undo, and checkpoints from this tab.</p>
<label class="check"><input id="draft-collection-private-ok" type="checkbox"><span>I understand this collection includes every saved article, source note, and private review question, and must be kept private.</span></label><button id="download-draft-collection" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Download private draft collection</button><p class="small">Only saved entries are included. Add or update current edits first. This unencrypted JSON file excludes checkpoints, collection undo, publishing profiles, and approvals. Check the saved file before leaving. Article exports still contain only the current article.</p>
<label for="load-draft-collection">Load a private collection to preview</label><input id="load-draft-collection" type="file" accept=".json,application/json" aria-describedby="draft-collection-file-help"><p id="draft-collection-file-help" class="small">Draft to Page collection JSON, up to 2 MiB and eight saved workspaces. It is read locally, not uploaded. A single-workspace backup belongs in Save or restore this workspace.</p>
<section id="draft-collection-file-preview" hidden aria-labelledby="draft-collection-file-heading"><h3 id="draft-collection-file-heading">Collection to load</h3><ol id="draft-collection-file-entries"></ol><p class="small">Loading replaces only the collection in this tab. It leaves the current editor unchanged. Open a saved article separately when ready.</p><div class="actions"><button id="apply-draft-collection" type="button" class="secondary" disabled>Load this collection</button><button id="cancel-draft-collection" type="button" class="secondary">Cancel collection preview</button></div></section>
</fieldset><p id="draft-collection-status" class="small" role="status" aria-live="polite">Draft collections are loading. Single-workspace backups and article exports remain available.</p>
<p class="small"><a href="/help/local-workspace/#draft-collections" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How private collections work (new tab)</a></p>
</details>
